   "source": [
    "<h1 style=\"margin-bottom: 7px;\"> Classical Image representation </h1>\n",
    "In the classical representation, a black and white image is a <b>matrix of integers</b>, where every position represent a pixel, and the integer represent the color intensity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "80865e3d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from PIL import Image\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "628b4e8f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "img = Image.open(\"test6.bmp\").convert('L')\n",
    "plt.imshow(img, cmap=\"gray\", extent=[0, 2, 2, 0])\n",
    "plt.xticks(range(0, 3))\n",
    "plt.yticks(range(0, 3))\n",
    "plt.colorbar()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ca38657d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The numpy array behind shows the image-encoding for classical computation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "a30c3798",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[[140  46]\n",
      " [ 89 192]]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(np.array(img))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d58d1fbe",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<br>\n",
    "<br>\n",
    "<br>\n",
    "\n",
    "<h1 style=\"margin-bottom: 7px;\">Novel Enhanced Quantum Representation (NEQR)</h1>\n",
    "The idea behind this approach for a quantistic image representation is to optimise memory by encoding all the the pixel into one single quantum register, taking advantage of the superposition property.\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "|I\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{Y=0}^{2^n-1} \\sum_{X=0}^{2^n-1} | f(Y, X) \\rangle \\otimes | YX \\rangle\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "**Where:**    \n",
    "- $| f(Y, X) \\rangle$ represents the grayscale intensity, also written as $|C^{i}_{YX}\\rangle$ \n",
    "- $| YX \\rangle$ represent the pixel position\n",
    "\n",
    "The Quantum Circuit creates a **superposition of the positional and color registers** for a $2^n\\times  2^n$ image."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "25da9a87",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<h2 style=\"margin-bottom: 3px;\">NEQR: Code Implementation</h2>\n",
    "<h2 style=\"margin-bottom: 3px;\">Image preparation</h2>\n",
    "By first, we create an array of bits by normalizing and converting the oginal matrix."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "ed177ed9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "bit_matrix_img = np.vectorize(lambda x: format(x, \"02b\"))(np.array(img) // 64)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "3e9f3337",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[['10' '00']\n",
      " ['01' '11']]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(bit_matrix_img)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1bf5462",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "To calculate the Qubits needed for the circuit the general formula is $q + 2n$  to represent a $2^n\\times  2^n$ image with gray range $2^{q}$.  \n",
    "In this case, we use a **2-bit color representation**, for 4 different levels of gray intensity. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "f49f122d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "img_width = len(bit_matrix_img) #since the image is square, width and height are the same\n",
    "n_positions = int(np.ceil(np.log2(img_width))*2)\n",
    "q = int(np.log2(4))\n",
    "\n",
    "n_qubits = n_positions + q"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "77f25d94",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "4, 2, 2\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(n_qubits, n_positions, q, sep=', ')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e81b1219",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<h2 style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\">First step</h2>\n",
    "To initialise the <b>Quantum Circuit</b>, all the Qubits must be set to $|0\\rangle$:  \n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "$$|\\psi\\rangle_{0} = |0\\rangle^{\\otimes2n+q}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "f462a76f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from qiskit import QuantumCircuit"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "b2d2e2f9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "qc = QuantumCircuit(n_qubits)\n",
    "initial_state = np.zeros(2**n_qubits)\n",
    "initial_state[0] = 1\n",
    "\n",
    "qc.initialize(initial_state, range(n_qubits));"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2aeb859f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "After the first step, the Quantum State is as follows:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "|\\psi\\rangle_0 = \n",
    "\\begin{bmatrix}\n",
    "1 \\\\\n",
    "0 \\\\\n",
    "\\vdots \\\\\n",
    "0\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "In this specific case, the image is $2px \\times 2px$, so the state has $2 + 2\\log_2 2 = 4$ Qubits."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fea6bbc7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<h2 style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\">Second step</h2>\n",
    "The position register is brought into a superposition state while the color registers remain unaltered.\n",
    "Formally, $U_1$ is applied, such that:\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "$$U_1 = I^{\\otimes q} \\otimes H^{\\otimes 2n}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "39d2e70e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The Quantum state after this operation can be written as:\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "$$|\\psi\\rangle_{1} = \\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{Y=0}^{2^n -1} \\sum_{X=0}^{2^n -1} |0\\rangle^{\\otimes q} |XY\\rangle$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "c0c81a89",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 538.33x367.889 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 10,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "for i in range(n_positions):\n",
    "    qc.h(i)\n",
    "    \n",
    "for i in range(n_positions, n_qubits):\n",
    "    qc.id(i)\n",
    "\n",
    "qc.draw('mpl', style='bw')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a848254e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In a probabilistic interpretation, the state can collapse with equal probability onto one of the position Qubits."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "244a626d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<h2 style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\">Third step</h2>\n",
    "The final step consists in setting the greyscale value for each pixel. Formally, $U_{YX}$ is applied, such that:\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "$$\n",
    "U_{YX}= \\Big(I \\otimes \\sum^{2^n -1}_{j=0} \\sum^{2^n -1}_{i=0, ji \\neq YX} |ji\\rangle \\langle ji| \\Big) + \\Omega_{YX} \\otimes |YX\\rangle \\langle YX|\n",
    "$$\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.3cm;\"></div>\n",
    "<h4 style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\">Detailed Analysis of the Operator $U_{YX}$</h4>\n",
    "The operator $U_{YX}$ can be decomposed into two different sub-operations to better understand its role. The <b>first sub-operation</b>, $U'_{YX}$, is written as follows:\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "$$U'_{YX} = \\Big(I \\otimes \\sum^{2^n -1}_{j=0} \\sum^{2^n -1}_{i=0, \\hspace{0.2em} ji \\neq YX} |ji\\rangle \\langle ji| \\Big)$$\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "This part handles all the pixels exepts for $YX$, leaving their quantum states unaffected. Inside the summation, we have a <b>projection operator</b> $|ji\\rangle \\langle ji|$, which, when applied to $|ji\\rangle$, results in  $|ji\\rangle$. If applied to any other state, it gives $0$. Formally:\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "$$\n",
    "|ji\\rangle \\langle ji||ab\\rangle = \n",
    "\\begin{cases}\n",
    "|ji\\rangle & \\scriptsize{if} \\hspace{0.5em} ab = ji \\\\\n",
    "0 & \\scriptsize{if} \\hspace{0.5em} ab \\neq ji\n",
    "\\end{cases}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7c8dea85",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The <b>second sub-operation</b>, $U''_{YX}$, is written as follows:\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.3cm;\"></div>\n",
    "$$\n",
    "U''_{YX} = \\Omega_{YX} \\otimes |YX\\rangle \\langle YX|\n",
    "$$\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.3cm;\"></div>\n",
    "The projection operator ensures that the greyscale transformation is applied only to the specific pixel $(Y,X)$. The operator $\\Omega_{YX}$ is the quantum operation designed for setting the greyscale levels for pixel $(Y,X)$:\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.3cm;\"></div>\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\Omega_{YX} = \\bigotimes^{q-1}_{i=0}\\Omega^i_{YX}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.3cm;\"></div>\n",
    "With $\\Omega^i_{YX}$ quantum oracles:\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.3cm;\"></div>\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\Omega^i_{YX}:|0\\rangle \\to \\Big\\vert \\hspace{0.2em} 0 \\oplus C^i_{YX}\\Big\\rangle\n",
    "$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d67a9b2b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "When the operator is applied to the initial quantum state, the result is:\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "$$\n",
    "U_{YX}(|\\psi\\rangle_{1}) = \\frac{1}{2^n} \\Big(\\sum_{j=0}^{2^n -1} \\sum_{i=0, \\hspace{0.2em}ji \\neq YX}^{2^n -1} |0\\rangle^{\\otimes q} |ji\\rangle + |f(Y,X)\\rangle |YX\\rangle \\Big)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "Since the operator $U_{YX}$ corresponds to a specific position, to determine the quantum state $|\\psi\\rangle_{2}$, $U_2$ is introduced, such that:\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "$$\n",
    "U_2 = \\prod^{2^n -1}_{Y=0} \\prod^{2^n -1}_{X=0} U_{YX}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "Thus, the final Quantum State is:\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "$$\n",
    "|\\psi\\rangle_2 = U_{2}(|\\psi\\rangle_{1}) = \\frac{1}{2^n} \\Big(\\sum_{Y=0}^{2^n -1} \\sum_{X=0}^{2^n -1} |f(Y,X)\\rangle |YX\\rangle \\Big)\n",
    "$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "774443a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "h, w = img_width, img_width\n",
    "\n",
    "for Y in range(h):\n",
    "    for X in range(w):\n",
    "        qc.barrier()\n",
    "        bin_Y = bin(Y)[2:].zfill(int(np.log2(h)))\n",
    "        bin_X = bin(X)[2:].zfill(int(np.log2(w)))\n",
    "        pos_bin =  bin_Y + bin_X\n",
    "        \n",
    "        for i, bit in enumerate(pos_bin):\n",
    "           if bit == '1':\n",
    "                qc.x(i)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        f_YX = bit_matrix_img[Y,X]  \n",
    "        control_qubits = [i for i, bit in enumerate(pos_bin) if bit == '1']\n",
    "        for i, bit in enumerate(f_YX[::-1]):\n",
    "           if bit == '1' and control_qubits != []:\n",
    "                qc.mcx(control_qubits, n_qubits-i-1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "393841c9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1834.55x451.5 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 12,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "qc.measure_all()\n",
    "qc.draw('mpl', style='bw', fold=35)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8e77bf66",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<h3>The final encoding</h3>\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "$$\n",
    "|\\psi\\rangle_2 = \\frac{1}{2^2} \\Big(|00\\rangle|10\\rangle + |01\\rangle|00\\rangle + |10\\rangle|01\\rangle + |11\\rangle|11\\rangle\\Big)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "<div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.4cm;\"></div>\n",
    "<h3>Getting the counts</h3>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "c9a035b5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from qiskit_aer import Aer\n",
    "from qiskit import transpile"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "6a86fecf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "simulator = Aer.get_backend('qasm_simulator')\n",
    "transpiled_circuit = transpile(qc, simulator)\n",
    "job = simulator.run(transpiled_circuit, shots=10000)\n",
    "res = job.result()\n",
    "counts = res.get_counts()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "7260c247-c269-4275-9372-3c317c6657c2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "{'1010': 2475, '1000': 2448, '1111': 2588, '0001': 2489} \n",
      "\n",
      " [['10' '00']\n",
      " ['01' '11']]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(counts, '\\n\\n', bit_matrix_img)\n",
    "#c0 c1 are the grey code\n",
    "#c2 c3 are Y X"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cc7cac65-3f58-4d0d-ab9f-681557fbbf3a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<h2> Are there any advantages?</h2>\n",
    "In this case the image has taken $2 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 8$<i>bits</i>, compared to the $4$<i>qubits</i> we used.<br> \n",
    "We now compare the formulas: \n",
    "$$ \\text{Bits} =w \\times h \\times q$$\n",
    "$$ \\hspace{17em}\\text{Qubits} =q + 2n \\hspace{2em}\\text{with} \\hspace{2em} n = \\lceil\\log_2(w)\\rceil = \\lceil\\log_2(h)\\rceil$$ \n",
    "Making the assumptions that we only operate with square images and with <i>q</i> fixed, we can plot the memory usage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "7ebdcd76-7958-43c2-a8fc-29121980037e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "q = 2\n",
    "wh_values = np.arange(2, 11, 2)\n",
    "n_qubits = q + 2 * np.ceil(np.log2(wh_values)).astype(int)\n",
    "n_bits = q * wh_values * wh_values"
   ]
  },
  {
